  <LanguagePacks><LanguagePack ID="ENU" IsDefault="true"><DisplayStrings><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.VMMS.Restart.Recovery"><Name>Restart VMMS when the management service monitor is critical</Name><Description>Disabled by default. Restarts the Virtual Machine Management Service when the VMMS monitor enters the Critical state; enable by override where automatic recovery is wanted.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.VmRuntime.Resume.Recovery"><Name>Resume the VM when its expected-state monitor is critical</Name><Description>Disabled by default. Runs Resume-VM for a VM that is paused (typically paused-critical after a storage outage) when the expected-state monitor is Critical; enable by override only where an automatic resume is safe.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.VmRuntime.Availability.Diagnostic"><Name>Capture VM health detail on state change</Name><Description>Runs the VM health probe when the expected-state monitor turns Critical and records every state and detail value in Health Explorer.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.VmInventory.Task"><Name>List virtual machines on this host</Name><Description>Get-VM: state, status, uptime, processors, memory, configuration version, cluster membership and start action for every VM on the host.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Headroom.Task"><Name>Show host resource headroom</Name><Description>Logical processors versus assigned virtual processors, physical memory versus assigned and demanded VM memory, NUMA topology and spanning.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.EventTail.Task"><Name>Show recent Hyper-V errors and warnings</Name><Description>The most recent Error/Warning events from the VMMS, Worker, Hypervisor, StorageVSP and Config admin channels. Parameter = number of events per channel (default 25).</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.LiveMigrationSettings.Task"><Name>Show live migration settings and recent migrations</Name><Description>Get-VMHost migration settings, migration networks and the last twenty live-migration events (20413, 20417, 21501, 21502, 21125, 21024).</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.SwitchConfiguration.Task"><Name>Show virtual switch, SET team and uplink configuration</Name><Description>Get-VMSwitch, Get-VMSwitchTeam, physical adapters with driver versions and RDMA state.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.PendingReboot.Task"><Name>Check for a pending reboot</Name><Description>Component Based Servicing, Windows Update and pending file-rename reboot flags plus the last boot time.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.PipelineSelfTest.Task"><Name>Run the monitoring pipeline self-test</Name><Description>PowerShell version and process, module availability (Hyper-V, FailoverClusters, Storage), hypervisor presence, VMMS/Host Compute/HealthService state and whether Get-VM succeeds under the agent account.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Bpa.Task"><Name>Run the Hyper-V Best Practices Analyzer</Name><Description>Invoke-BpaModel Microsoft/Windows/Hyper-V and list non-compliant Warning and Error results.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.RestartVmms.Task"><Name>Remediation: Restart the Virtual Machine Management Service</Name><Description>Restart-Service vmms. Running VMs keep running; management operations pause for a few seconds.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.RestartVmCompute.Task"><Name>Remediation: Restart the Host Compute Service</Name><Description>Restart-Service vmcompute. Do not run while VM operations are in progress.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.VmRuntime.Detail.Task"><Name>Show virtual machine detail</Name><Description>Configuration, integration services, network adapters with VLAN and IP, virtual hard disks with the full VHD chain and AVHDX sizes, and checkpoints.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.VmRuntime.Performance.Task"><Name>Show virtual machine performance snapshot</Name><Description>Measure-VM resource metering when enabled, plus live virtual processor and Dynamic Memory pressure counters.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.VmRuntime.Replica.Task"><Name>Show Hyper-V Replica status</Name><Description>Get-VMReplication and Measure-VMReplication for the VM.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.VmRuntime.Start.Task"><Name>Remediation: Start the virtual machine</Name><Description>Start-VM.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.VmRuntime.Stop.Task"><Name>Remediation: Shut down the virtual machine</Name><Description>Stop-VM -Force (guest shutdown through integration services; turns the VM off if the guest does not respond).</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.VmRuntime.Save.Task"><Name>Remediation: Save the virtual machine state</Name><Description>Save-VM.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.VmRuntime.Resume.Task"><Name>Remediation: Resume a paused virtual machine</Name><Description>Resume-VM. Use after the storage behind a paused-critical VM has been restored.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.VmRuntime.Restart.Task"><Name>Remediation: Restart the virtual machine</Name><Description>Restart-VM -Force.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.VmRuntime.MergeCheckpoints.Task"><Name>Remediation: Remove all checkpoints and merge the VHD chain</Name><Description>Remove-VMSnapshot for every checkpoint; the merge continues in the background.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.VmRuntime.CreateCheckpoint.Task"><Name>Remediation: Create a checkpoint</Name><Description>Checkpoint-VM with a timestamped name.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.VmRuntime.ResumeReplication.Task"><Name>Remediation: Resume Hyper-V Replica</Name><Description>Resume-VMReplication.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.VmRuntime.MoveToBestNode.Task"><Name>Remediation: Live migrate the clustered VM to the best node</Name><Description>Move-ClusterVirtualMachineRole -MigrationType Live; the cluster chooses the destination.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Task.WriteAction"><Name>HyperVPrivateCloud task runner</Name><Description>Runs the operator task script for this capability through PowerShell 7 on the agent and returns its text output.</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.Vmms.Collection.Rule"><Name>Collect Microsoft-Windows-Hyper-V-VMMS-Admin errors and warnings</Name><Description>Collects Error, Critical and Warning events from the Microsoft-Windows-Hyper-V-VMMS-Admin channel (Virtual Machine Management Service) into the operational database and the Data Warehouse so the Hyper-V host and VM event views and reports have data.</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.Worker.Collection.Rule"><Name>Collect Microsoft-Windows-Hyper-V-Worker-Admin errors and warnings</Name><Description>Collects Error, Critical and Warning events from the Microsoft-Windows-Hyper-V-Worker-Admin channel (Hyper-V worker process) into the operational database and the Data Warehouse so the Hyper-V host and VM event views and reports have data.</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.Hypervisor.Collection.Rule"><Name>Collect Microsoft-Windows-Hyper-V-Hypervisor-Admin errors and warnings</Name><Description>Collects Error, Critical and Warning events from the Microsoft-Windows-Hyper-V-Hypervisor-Admin channel (hypervisor) into the operational database and the Data Warehouse so the Hyper-V host and VM event views and reports have data.</Description></DisplayString>
