    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.HypervisorNotRunning.Alert.Rule.AlertMessage"><Name>Hyper-V hypervisor is not running</Name><Description>Event {0} on the Hyper-V host: {1}</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.WorkerError.Alert.Rule"><Name>Hyper-V worker process reported an error for a virtual machine</Name><Description>The Hyper-V worker process (vmwp.exe) logged an Error or Critical event for a virtual machine. These events cover VM crashes, resets, failed starts and unrecoverable virtual-processor errors, and normally mean a VM is down or was restarted.</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.WorkerError.Alert.Rule.AlertMessage"><Name>Hyper-V worker process reported an error for a virtual machine</Name><Description>Event {0} on the Hyper-V host: {1}</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.VmmsError.Alert.Rule"><Name>Hyper-V Virtual Machine Management Service reported an error</Name><Description>The Virtual Machine Management Service (VMMS) logged an Error or Critical event other than a live-migration failure, for example a VM that failed to start or initialize, a configuration that could not be loaded, a checkpoint or export failure, or a Hyper-V Replica error.</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.VmmsError.Alert.Rule.AlertMessage"><Name>Hyper-V Virtual Machine Management Service reported an error</Name><Description>Event {0} on the Hyper-V host: {1}</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.HypervisorError.Alert.Rule"><Name>Hyper-V hypervisor reported an error</Name><Description>The hypervisor itself logged an Error, Critical or Warning event. Hypervisor errors are rare and affect every virtual machine on the host: launch failures, microcode or firmware problems, and partition-level faults.</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.HypervisorError.Alert.Rule.AlertMessage"><Name>Hyper-V hypervisor reported an error</Name><Description>Event {0} on the Hyper-V host: {1}</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.StorageVspError.Alert.Rule"><Name>Hyper-V virtual storage provider reported an I/O error</Name><Description>The Hyper-V storage virtualization service provider (StorageVSP) logged an Error or Critical event. This is I/O between a virtual machine and its VHDX, VHD or pass-through disk failing on the host side and is the earliest host-visible sign of virtual disk data loss.</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.StorageVspError.Alert.Rule.AlertMessage"><Name>Hyper-V virtual storage provider reported an I/O error</Name><Description>Event {0} on the Hyper-V host: {1}</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.VmSwitchError.Alert.Rule"><Name>Hyper-V virtual switch reported an error</Name><Description>The Hyper-V virtual switch logged an Error or Critical event, for example a physical uplink binding failure, a switch extension failure or a port that could not be created. Virtual machines on the switch may lose connectivity.</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.VmSwitchError.Alert.Rule.AlertMessage"><Name>Hyper-V virtual switch reported an error</Name><Description>Event {0} on the Hyper-V host: {1}</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.HighAvailabilityError.Alert.Rule"><Name>Hyper-V clustered virtual machine high-availability error</Name><Description>The Hyper-V high-availability component logged an Error or Critical event for a clustered virtual machine role, such as a failed online, a failed move or a configuration that the cluster cannot reach.</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.HighAvailabilityError.Alert.Rule.AlertMessage"><Name>Hyper-V clustered virtual machine high-availability error</Name><Description>Event {0} on the Hyper-V host: {1}</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.ComputeError.Alert.Rule"><Name>Hyper-V Host Compute Service reported an error</Name><Description>The Host Compute Service (vmcompute) logged an Error or Critical event. Modern Hyper-V VM and container operations route through this service; errors indicate failed compute system creation, start or configuration.</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.ComputeError.Alert.Rule.AlertMessage"><Name>Hyper-V Host Compute Service reported an error</Name><Description>Event {0} on the Hyper-V host: {1}</Description></DisplayString>
    <DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Host.Event.ConfigError.Alert.Rule"><Name>Hyper-V virtual machine configuration error</Name><Description>The Hyper-V configuration store logged an Error or Critical event: a VM configuration file (.vmcx/.vmrs) could not be read, written or is corrupt. The VM may fail to start or lose settings.</Description></DisplayString>
